# Real FDC catalog exports and the real (non-commercial-licensed)
# PhyFoodComp workbook — large and/or not redistributable, see
# backend/app/ingest_phytate.py's module docstring.
/data/

# PhyFoodComp source-derived review/mapping artifacts — contain verbatim
# source food descriptions and reported phytate values, not just reviewer
# decisions or code. source_licence_policy.py currently records
# redistribution_permitted=False/export_permitted=False for PhyFoodComp;
# these must not be publicly tracked while that holds (see PROMPT 9 in
# prompts.txt and docs/phytate-review/PRIVATE_ARTIFACTS.md). An authorised
# operator supplies these files locally at the same paths — every CLI tool
# that reads them already accepts an explicit override flag
# (--mapping-csv/--review-dir/--stable-id-mapping), so no code change is
# needed to use them from outside the repository.
#
# Explicit paths, not a glob — docs/phytate-review/ also holds files that
# are safe to keep public (stable_id_exceptions*.csv,
# stable_id_duplicates_still_needing_review.csv, the *.py tooling): a
# broad */*.csv pattern would silently swallow those too.
/docs/phytate-review/final_approved_mapping.csv
/docs/phytate-review/stable_id_mapping.csv
/docs/phytate-review/review_1_ambiguous.csv
/docs/phytate-review/review_2_no_candidate.csv
/docs/phytate-review/review_3_branded_low_confidence.csv
/docs/phytate-review/review_4_special_cases.csv
/docs/phytate-review/review_5_infant_flour_cluster.csv
/docs/phytate-review/review_6_accepted_sample.csv
/docs/phytate-review/review_6b_accepted_remainder.csv
/docs/phytate-review/prompt3b_bug_evidence_and_fixtures.csv
/docs/phytate-review/pre-3b-baseline/
